When we upgraded to PL6 of nethack 3.0 we started have very long delays
when throwing or after hitting something intrinsically resistant.  After
reading a recent post I checked a few things about our setup (a Sun4 running
SunOS 4.0.3).  A stty -a indicates ixon -ixany -ixoff -ofill.  Given the
-ofill setting I wasn't surprised when setting the nonull option had no effect.
Our man page listed a time parameter for stty but didn't indicate what it
controlled (setting it to 0 had no effect).  We rarely play nethack on
the console or the one physical tty on the machine - it is usually over
the network to other Sun's that have other physical devices.  Does it
matter if the stty is executed on the machine where the game is running
or the machine with the actually tty?  Any suggestions would be appreciated.


